    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31650" root="غرد" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اغرود</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اغرودة</span> [i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُغْرُودٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُغْرُودَةٌ</span>, in
measure like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُسْلُوبٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُحْدُوثَةٌ</span>,] <i>A song</i> or <i>a
singing</i> [or <i>a warbling,</i> of a bird, &amp;c.]: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَغَارِيدُ</span>.
(Har p. 445.) One says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَائِرٌ مُسْتَمْلَحُ الأَغَارِيدِ</span>
[<i>A bird whose songs,</i> or <i>warblings, are esteemed
sweet</i>]. (A.)

